<TSL-SYSTEM Terminal> $trunc, A command which makes TSL-users can execute external commands.
Usage: trunc COMMAND

Calling external command(From Mother System).
SuperUser permission is required before executing this command.

The command is passed to the shell of the mother system:
    Windows:    cmd /C COMMAND
    Linux:      /bin/sh -c COMMAND

Command Options:
    COMMAND,          External System Command.

Exit Status:
    0,        The external command finished successfully.
    Other,    The external command finished with failure, and its exit code
              is printed before the next prompt.

Examples:
    trunc dir
    trunc echo TSL-SYSTEM
    trunc python --version
    trunc python -c "import os"

Arguments containing spaces follow the quoting rules of the shell above.

